    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini-pick\n\n### Description\n\nI'm trying to use grep_live on a decently sized Repository. 6000 or so files.\r\nIt starts off fine, working as intended, but within a few characters neovim entirely \"hangs\", won't accept input anymore and can only be forcably closed.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI'm running a basically \"mini only\" nvim config. Lazy.nvim is used to pull mini, other than that, it's only settings for tabs, spaces and some indenting.\r\nThis is running on Windows 11 natively (no WSL or such). I can't really try to reproduce this on linux, as the Repo is work only and i don't have a work Linux machine kicking around.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\ngrep_live should continue working.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nNeovim entirely locks up and only killing the terminal solves this.",
