            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI kind of can reproduce this, but not quite. I am using [chromium/chromium](https://github.com/chromium/chromium) to do a `grep_live`. When pressing single `l` it does hang after a while with something like \"E41: out of memory\" error. And the issue seems to be that Neovim/libuv/'mini.pick' can't easily process the amount of matched lines. So `rg` works as it should and processing its output to stdout results into too big object.\r\n\r\nI don't think I can do much here besides limiting the amount of matched items, which I don't really want to do. Instead caution users to not make many matches.\r\n\r\nJust to be sure, could you clarify some things:\r\n- Does plain `rg` work for you? Navigate to the repo and run the following command: \r\n```bash\r\nrg --column --line-number --no-heading --hidden --no-follow --color=never --smart-case -- <enter your pattern>\r\n```\r\n   Does it finish and not get stuck?\r\n- Does typing quickly until you get to a bigger version of a pattern work?",
