            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Since you mentioned that you're on Windows 11 and using WSL. I had a similar issue where typing in `grep_live` would lag or hang Neovim.\r\n\r\nWSL has 2 versions. WSL1 and WSL2. WSL2 which I think installs by default on Windows 11 runs in a VM with a full Linux kernel and a network share to access the Windows file system. The downside is it has pretty terrible performance with the file system.\r\nYou can read more about it here: [Comparing WSL Versions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/compare-versions)\r\n\r\nWhat worked for me was switching to WSL1 from WSL2. It improved my overall performance with `rg`, `fzf` and others.\r\n\r\nYou can see which version you're running in powershell: `wsl --list --verbose`\r\nAnd to switch WSL versions you do: `wsl --set-version <Name> 1` where the number at the end is the version you want to switch to.\r\n\r\nDo note that doing this might break some things within WSL. So far I haven't had any problems other than the system clipboard `clipboard=unnamedplus`. I use `win32yank` so the solution for that was to remove it from within WSL and place it in `$PATH` under Windows.",
