            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Does plain rg work for you? Navigate to the repo and run the following command:\r\n\r\nYes. And it does with a high number of matches. Let's say i want to search for \"company_apt_cacher\" in my repo. git_live usually hangs after \"company\", which seems like around the time first matches are shown. plain rg in Terminal can find matches for just \"company\" fine though.\r\ngrep_live also works with less common search terms.\r\n\r\nAnother \"Idea\": Part of the repo is a git lfs store. So there are some bigger files in there, and some binaries. Maybe those are an issue. I might configure rg to ignore a bunch of folders and filetypes. I never need to match anything in those folders anyways. They are just part of the repo, but not needed for coding.\r\n\r\n> Does typing quickly until you get to a bigger version of a pattern work?\r\n\r\nNo. But it might be that i'm not typing fast enough\r\n\r\nFor now MiniPicker.builtin.grep() works for me to get my whole searchterm in. As long as it doesn't match a bajillion things, this is fine. Of note though: Putting just \"company\" into Mini Pick grep() opens the UI but shows no results and also crashes neovim.",
