            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hmm... I'll think about this, but honestly not sure how to help here. I can reproduce *some* hang, but only on a much bigger repo (400K files against 6K).\r\n\r\nLet's try to get some more information (in as much details as you can provide due to privacy stuff):\r\n- How many files are there?\r\n- What is the size of the repo inside which search is done (to get a rough idea of how many lines are being searched)?\r\n- How many matches does plain `rg` in terminal show for the case that breaks `grep_live` (the \"company\" pattern, I believe)? Please, make sure to use the command from [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/522#issuecomment-1764845220).\r\n- How many matches does the working example have (the \"company_apt_cacher\" one)?\r\n\r\n> Another \"Idea\": Part of the repo is a git lfs store. So there are some bigger files in there, and some binaries. Maybe those are an issue. I might configure rg to ignore a bunch of folders and filetypes. I never need to match anything in those folders anyways. They are just part of the repo, but not needed for coding.\r\n\r\nBy default `rg` ignores binary files, though. Maybe they are treated as *very long* string and processing this string leads to memory overuse?",
