            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> How many files are there?\r\n\r\ngit ls | wc -l shows 4351 files\r\n\r\n> What is the size of the repo inside which search is done (to get a rough idea of how many lines are being searched)?\r\n\r\nOur gitlab instace claims 6.8 GB Project Storage. du -sh say 7.5 GB\r\n\r\n> How many matches does plain rg in terminal show\r\n\r\nrg into wc -l says 4184 Matches\r\n\r\n> How many matches does the working example have (the \"company_apt_cacher\" one)?\r\n\r\n37\r\n\r\nI have noticed a couple of 100MB plus SQL files. Adding a glob option to ripgrep's config to exclude all SQL files ( `--glob=!*.sql` ) seems to have fixed this entirely. I still get 3600 Matches, but everything is working fine for me now. It might be, that trying to preview these large files with maybe extremely long line causes the issue, and not the amount of matches. Excluding those SQL files is completely fine for me, as i never have to search in those.\r\n\r\n",
