            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the detailed info!\r\n\r\nYes, having number of matches in the vicinity of 5000 should be totally fine and not crash. And yes, it does seem that for some reason `rg` tries to search inside those SQL files, finds match, and tries to preview long lines.\r\n\r\nI would be really grateful if you could confirm this for sure. Could you add something like `--max-columns=100` to your ripgrep's config and try using `grep_live` with it available? Will it works and show \"[Omitted long line with x matches]\" instead of long lines? And are those lines indeed form SQL files?",
